sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WebXR on the flat stereo display (ORDER 194, 195): three modes the
    person picks from the page's context menu (3D Display: flat TV or
    output, flat headset, VR over the phone; dom.vr.flat.mode), the
    separation from libstereo-policy's display depth (the display's kind and
    physical size, with the person's strength and screen plane on top:
    dom.vr.flat.depth-strength, dom.vr.flat.screen-plane-mm), Escape always
    ends the session (WebXR 4.1), a visible Exit control, the mode's name and
    an entry hint drawn by the browser, the mouse and keyboard in the flat
    modes, and the keyboard focus kept across a session.
  * A session that ends while a frame is in flight no longer leaves the VR
    submit thread polling for ever: the browser quits. Measured: 100 enters
    and leaves with the keyboard (ten runs of ten) quit cleanly; before, two
    runs in eight hung.
  * CSS depth (ORDER 414): the property depth (sunk | screen | popped |
    <percentage> | <number>), the words Union, Stereo KWin and SVGStereo share,
    parsed and computed, not inherited; layout.css.depth.enabled is off until
    the browser draws an element once per view at its depth.
  * The 3D Display menu, the overlay and the 3D Video and 3D Canvas menus in
    the edition's nine languages (German added).
  * Depends on libstereo-policy1 (>= 1.15.0), which has the display depth.
  * The source states what it is: browser commit 81fecb57fb (Sparky-OS/waterfox,
    branch stereo3d) in SOURCE.edition.json, debian/browser-build.env and the
    vendor baseline.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

